From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 06 Sep 2026 01:20:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virgl: enumerate dma-buf format modifiers

pipe_screen::query_dmabuf_modifiers was never implemented for virgl, so it stayed NULL and
dri2_query_dma_buf_modifiers() (src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c:1745) returned a count of
zero for every format:

    if (pscreen->query_dmabuf_modifiers != NULL) {
       pscreen->query_dmabuf_modifiers(...);
       ...
    } else {
       *count = 0;
    }

A Wayland compositor running on virgl therefore advertises only the implicit modifier. On a
Raspberry Pi 5 with an AGL cluster in a Xen DomU, weston-simple-dmabuf-feedback shows exactly
that -- all 34 formats as "modifier NONE_INVALID (0xffffffffffffff)" and nothing else.

The consequence lands on guest Vulkan. Venus' WSI, finding no modifiers, takes the legacy path
in vn_wsi.c which forces DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR on scanout images -- it says so when run with
VN_DEBUG=wsi:

    MESA-VIRTIO: debug: forcing scanout image linear (no explicit modifier support)

and that path carries its own TODO ("We should require modifier support at some point"). The
host GPU is tiled, so it then re-tiles the linear image once per frame in order to sample it.
Measured with V3D_DEBUG=perf on the host: 2122 occurrences of

    Updating 1920x1080@0 shadow for linear texture

in 40 s of a 54 fps cluster -- one 1920x1080 conversion per frame, about 7.9 MiB, and the only
reason the TFU engine shows up at all in the Vulkan lane (0.98 jobs/frame against exactly zero
on both OpenGL lanes).

virgl_is_dmabuf_modifier_supported() already returns true for *any* modifier, with a comment
saying so, and virgl_get_dmabuf_modifier_planes() already answers plane queries. Enumeration
was the only missing piece.

Multi-planar formats are deliberately excluded: virgl resolves aux planes on the host, and
venus separately refuses modifiers whose memory-plane count differs from the format plane
count (vn_GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2), so advertising them would only produce a
rejection later.

Why advertising a tiled modifier from the GUEST is safe here, which is the obvious
objection: the modifier only decides what the guest's WSI asks the compositor for, and
the buffer itself is still allocated by the host through venus. When vrend imports it
the modifier travels with the dma-buf as an EGL attribute
(EGL_LINUX_DMA_BUF_EXT/EGL_DMA_BUF_PLANE0_MODIFIER_*), so host and guest cannot
disagree about the layout -- which is why the mid-draw screenshots below show a
correct picture rather than tile noise.

The limitation is the other direction: a GL client in the same guest that uses dma-buf
feedback now sees BROADCOM_UIF advertised too, and nothing here checks that the host
can import it. On this platform it can, because the host IS Broadcom.

XXX This is a proof of concept, not a finished driver. The correct modifier list is the host
renderer's, and virgl cannot ask for it -- union virgl_caps carries no modifier table.
Productising this needs a caps addition on the virglrenderer side so the guest enumerates what
the host can actually allocate and import. Until then the list is LINEAR (always valid) plus
the Broadcom UIF modifier this platform's host GPU uses, which is enough to test whether the
rest of the chain -- weston advertisement, venus modifier selection, host V3DV allocation,
host V3D import -- lights up.

Verified on the platform described above, AGL instrument cluster at 1080x1920 fullscreen in a
Xen DomU, 40 s window, frame rate counted from wl_surface.commit in WAYLAND_DEBUG:

  * weston-simple-dmabuf-feedback now lists LINEAR (0x0) and BROADCOM_UIF
    (0x700000000000006) per format, where before every format had only NONE_INVALID.
  * The Vulkan client's buffers arrive with the tiled modifier -- zwp_linux_buffer_params_v1
    .add() carries hi=117440512 lo=6 (BROADCOM_UIF), against hi=16777215 lo=4294967295
    (DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID) before. Checked directly, because venus no longer logging
    "forcing scanout image linear" only proves the legacy path was skipped, not that a tiled
    modifier was chosen.
  * VN_DEBUG=init,wsi shows the wsi debug channel live (swapchain created/acquired) with the
    linear-forcing line absent.
  * The host's per-frame re-tile is gone: v3d-jobs tfu 0.98/frame -> 0.0, and the cost of a
    render job falls 1.25 ms -> 0.95 ms.
  * Vulkan reaches the OpenGL lane's frame rate -- 54.0 -> 60.0 fps, with the host GPU's
    render engine at 75.3 % against the OpenGL lane's 80.4 %.
  * The cluster still renders correctly. This is the check that matters for a patch that
    advertises a modifier the host was never asked about: a UIF/linear mismatch corrupts the
    image while every counter above improves, so screenshots were taken mid-draw on both the
    Vulkan and the OpenGL lane. Neither shows an artefact, and the OpenGL lane -- which
    shares this driver through the compositor -- holds 60.0 fps unchanged.

Upstream: not submitted.
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [proof of concept]
 Not submittable as written, and the patch's own XXX says why: the modifier list
 belongs to the host renderer and virgl has no way to ask for it (union virgl_caps
 carries no modifier table). Productising it needs a virglrenderer caps addition
 first; the hardcoded LINEAR + BROADCOM_UIF list here exists to test whether the
 rest of the chain lights up.
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
@@ -35,6 +35,8 @@
 #include "vl/vl_decoder.h"
 #include "vl/vl_video_buffer.h"
 
+#include "drm-uapi/drm_fourcc.h"
+
 #include "virgl_screen.h"
 #include "virgl_resource.h"
 #include "virgl_public.h"
@@ -1092,6 +1094,61 @@
    return true;
 }
 
+/* virgl never enumerated modifiers, so pipe_screen::query_dmabuf_modifiers stayed NULL and
+ * dri2_query_dma_buf_modifiers() (src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri2.c) returned a count of zero
+ * for every format. A Wayland compositor running on virgl therefore advertised only the
+ * implicit modifier, and a guest Vulkan (venus) client's WSI, finding no modifiers, fell back
+ * to the legacy path in vn_wsi.c which forces DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR on scanout images
+ * ("forcing scanout image linear (no explicit modifier support)"). On a tiled GPU the host
+ * then re-tiles that linear image once per frame so it can be sampled -- measured on a
+ * Raspberry Pi 5 as one 1920x1080 "shadow for linear texture" conversion per frame.
+ *
+ * Note that virgl_is_dmabuf_modifier_supported() above already accepts *any* modifier, so the
+ * only thing that was missing is the enumeration.
+ *
+ * XXX The list below is a proof of concept, not a finished driver. The correct list is the
+ * host renderer's, and virgl has no way to ask for it: union virgl_caps carries no modifier
+ * table. Productising this needs a caps addition on the virglrenderer side so the guest can
+ * enumerate what the host can actually allocate and import. Until then this advertises
+ * LINEAR (always valid) plus the Broadcom UIF modifier this platform's host GPU uses.
+ */
+static void
+virgl_query_dmabuf_modifiers(UNUSED struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
+                             enum pipe_format format,
+                             int max,
+                             uint64_t *modifiers,
+                             unsigned int *external_only,
+                             int *count)
+{
+   static const uint64_t supported[] = {
+      DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
+      DRM_FORMAT_MOD_BROADCOM_UIF,
+   };
+   const int num = ARRAY_SIZE(supported);
+
+   /* Multi-planar formats are out of scope: virgl resolves aux planes on the host, and
+    * venus additionally refuses modifiers whose memory-plane count differs from the format
+    * plane count (vn_GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2). Advertise nothing for them
+    * rather than something that will be rejected later.
+    */
+   if (util_format_get_num_planes(format) != 1) {
+      *count = 0;
+      return;
+   }
+
+   if (max <= 0) {
+      *count = num;
+      return;
+   }
+
+   *count = MIN2(max, num);
+   for (int i = 0; i < *count; i++) {
+      modifiers[i] = supported[i];
+      if (external_only)
+         external_only[i] = 0;
+   }
+}
+
 static unsigned int
 virgl_get_dmabuf_modifier_planes(UNUSED struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
                                  UNUSED uint64_t modifier,
@@ -1199,6 +1256,7 @@
    screen->base.fence_get_fd = virgl_fence_get_fd;
    screen->base.query_memory_info = virgl_query_memory_info;
    screen->base.get_disk_shader_cache = virgl_get_disk_shader_cache;
+   screen->base.query_dmabuf_modifiers = virgl_query_dmabuf_modifiers;
    screen->base.is_dmabuf_modifier_supported = virgl_is_dmabuf_modifier_supported;
    screen->base.get_dmabuf_modifier_planes = virgl_get_dmabuf_modifier_planes;
 
